From 83062cf408d11a6581c5bfde72fd0a3f063cdde0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:57:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 67/72] hw/display/pvg: render mip-chain levels in place; flush
 only what blits touch

The Wallpaper pane's blur pyramid renders into each level of a private
mip-chain texture and then samples the chain. Each level had its own host
image, so every frame flushed each level to guest memory and re-uploaded
the chain (~290 flushes / 620 MiB per 500 cmdbufs). Private 2D targets
inside a mip chain now render through a level view of the chain's own
image (GENERAL layout), which sampling uses directly: 0 flushes.

Blit segments flushed every private texture of the task; they now flush
only the ranges each copy reads or writes. Per-level/slice host images
carry level and slice in the key. Flush reasons are logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
